  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Masquerade lives on</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Masquerade , an African survival is seen erroneously as a stage item. It is a costumed dance street theatre performance but the tradition is defunct. Fragmented stragglers in costume are tragically incompetent and inadequate. They appear to know little about the raison d&#x2019;&#xea;tre for this ancestral art form and are treated as nuisances . Former Minister of Culture, Dr. Anthony said many have &#x2018;looked down&#x2019; on this art form, maybe because they were not aware of its rich historical and traditional value and importance to Guyanese heritage. If the culture is allowed to diminish, Guyanese will eventually lose their identity.</narrative>
  </description>
